---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const title = 'Privacy Policy | Exhibit Automation';
const description =
  "How we collect, use and retain information from visitors and clients, including call recordings, transcripts and messaging consent.";
---

<Base title={title} description={description} path="/legal/privacy">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap legal">
      <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      {/* Not yet reviewed by counsel. Get it reviewed before signing the first client. */}
      <p class="small">Last updated: September 2026.</p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>Exhibit Automation ("we") is a business operated by its founder, Afan Rashid. We build and operate automated operations workflows for small businesses. Contact: <a href="mailto:hello@joinexhibit.com">hello@joinexhibit.com</a>.</p>

      <h2>Website visitors</h2>
      <p>This website does not use analytics, advertising or tracking cookies. It loads fonts from Google Fonts, and the booking calendar on our intro-call page is provided by Cal.com; both have their own privacy policies. If you submit the fit-check form we collect the information you enter (name, email, phone, business details and your answers) to respond to your request. If you book an intro call, those details and answers are passed to Cal.com, our scheduling provider, to create the booking. We do not sell this information or add you to marketing lists without your consent.</p>

      <h2>Business contacts we reach out to</h2>
      <p>We may contact property management and other service businesses about our services using contact details they publish, such as the email address or phone number on their website. We keep the company name, those public contact details, the software their website indicates they use, and a record of our correspondence. Every email includes a way to opt out; if you reply "unsubscribe" or ask us to stop, we record that and do not contact you again. You can also email <a href="mailto:hello@joinexhibit.com">hello@joinexhibit.com</a> to have your details deleted.</p>

      <h2>Clients and their customers</h2>
      <p>When we operate a workflow for a client, we process information on the client's behalf and under the client's instructions, including: call audio and transcripts, emails and text messages, and records from the client's business systems (for example property-management, field-service or practice-management software). We process this information only to perform the agreed workflow.</p>

      <h2>Call recording and transcription</h2>
      <p>Calls handled by the agent may be recorded and transcribed. Where required by law, callers hear a recording notice at the start of the call. Some states, including Maryland, require the consent of every party to a call before it is recorded. Clients are responsible for confirming that the notice configuration meets the requirements where they and their callers are located; we provide a default notice and configure it per client.</p>

      <h2>Text messaging</h2>
      <p>Automated text messages are sent only to people who have contacted the client first (for example, a leasing inquiry or a service request) and only about that inquiry. Every message includes a way to opt out. We do not send marketing texts.</p>

      <h2>Health information</h2>
      <p>We do not knowingly process protected health information and do not serve clients whose workflows involve it.</p>

      <h2>Retention</h2>
      <p>Call recordings and transcripts are retained for 90 days by default and then deleted, unless the client requests a different period or the law requires longer. Structured records written to the client's systems belong to the client and follow the client's retention policies.</p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>We limit access to client information to the people and systems that need it to run the workflow. Credentials for a client's business software stay on our own servers and are never included in messages to AI platforms. A client can revoke our access at any time from their own software. If we become aware of a security incident affecting a client's information, we will notify that client without undue delay.</p>

      <h2>Sub-processors</h2>
      <p>We use third-party infrastructure to operate workflows, including the AI platform the agent runs on, telephony and messaging providers, and hosting. We use Cal.com to schedule intro calls. A current list is available on request.</p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>Our website and services are for businesses and are not directed to children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children.</p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>You may ask what information we hold about you, ask us to correct or delete it, or object to processing, by emailing <a href="mailto:hello@joinexhibit.com">hello@joinexhibit.com</a>. If you are a customer of one of our clients, we may direct your request to that client.</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>We will post any changes on this page and update the date above.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero { padding: 64px 0; }
  .legal { max-width: 760px; }
  .legal h2 { font-size: 1.25rem; margin-top: 2em; }
</style>
